From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 11:47:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gpl: a routability phase whose minimum is its first pass ends
 on it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A routability pass measures the congestion of one placement, and the
phase keeps the minimum: revertToMinCongestion() puts back the sizes,
target density, fillers and net weights of the pass that measured the
least. When the phase ended by going back to it (GPL-0053, GPL-0054,
GPL-0091, GPL-0097), runRoutability() put the cells on the routability
snapshot, taken on the way down at overflow 0.60, and the placement
descended again from there with the minimum's sizes. No pass measured
the congestion of that descent: the phase ended on a placement nobody
measured, and the replay cannot reproduce the one that was (the
timing-driven iterations and the density penalty's one-shot change are
spent, and it starts with the snapshot's momentum).

A minimum at pass 1 means no inflation helped. What a pass that finds
nothing to fix produces (GPL-0090) is the right ending then: the
placement it measured, its sizes, and on from there. Since a settle wait
still open at the target overflow ends there and runs its pass
(GPL-0124), that is what XiangShan's XSTile parent does: pass 1
measured 1.1637 on the placement that had converged at iteration 521
(overflow 0.0894),
passes 2 to 4 at overflow 0.30 read 1.94, 1.35 and 1.21, and GPL-0054
went back to the snapshot of iteration 380. The new descent converged
at iteration 914 with congestion 1.3611 and HPWL 60.3 M um, against
1.1363 and 56.1 M for a run with no pass.

runRoutability() now saves a second snapshot just before pass 1: each
region's placement and Nesterov state, with the overflow and HPWL
updateNextIter() measured on it (NesterovBase::saveFirstPassSnapshot(),
and IoPinBase's pins with it), and the loop's momentum and wirelength
coefficients. It is kept parallel to the gcells through filler cuts and
restores, as the routability snapshot is, and released when the phase
ends. RouteBase records the pass that measured the minimum
(getMinRcPass()). When the phase ends by going back to its minimum and
that is pass 1, the cells go back to the second snapshot instead
(GPL-0125), with the overflow measured there, which is therefore not
stale: at or below the target overflow the placement converges on it in
the same iteration, and above it the descent goes on from it. The
density goes back onto the look-ahead (SLP) coordinates, not the
coordinates: nesterovUpdateCoordinates() puts it there, and the
overflow, HPWL and RUDY pass 1 measured were read there. So the phase
ends exactly on what pass 1 measured; on the coordinates, medium01's
bins read an overflow of 0.1028 against the 0.0999 restored, above its
target of 0.10.

What changes, and what does not:

- Only a placement whose routability phase ends by going back to a
  minimum at pass 1. That includes a phase that ends on pass 1 itself
  (GPL-0053 or GPL-0097 there): it stays on the placement pass 1
  measured instead of going back to the snapshot.
- A phase with no pass, one that meets the congestion target (GPL-0090)
  and one whose minimum is a later pass are as before, and so is a
  divergence recovery (GPL-0112), which goes back to the routability
  snapshot on purpose. Every phase with a pass pays for a copy of four
  vectors per region, from pass 1 to the end of the phase.
- A minimum at a later pass k still goes on from the routability
  snapshot, with pass k's sizes. Keeping pass k's placement as well
  would change placements where the passes help, and is not done here.

Tests, in routability_minimum_test, on gcd, driving the real controller
in the main loop's order. Between passes the test places every gcell,
fillers included, on a lattice of the pass's own, with the look-ahead
coordinates one site right of the coordinates and the density on them,
and gives each pass its own gradients, step length, density penalty and
HPWL:

- FirstPassMinimumAtTargetEndsOnItsPlacement: pass 1 at the target
  overflow, run by GPL-0124, then three passes that read worse. The
  density sees the cells on pass 1's look-ahead coordinates, every gcell
  and the region have the Nesterov state of pass 1, the cells have its
  sizes, overflow and HPWL, RUDY on them at pass 1's wire width reads
  pass 1's congestion, and the placement converges in that iteration.
  Without the change every cell is on the snapshot, the overflow is
  stale and it does not converge.
- FirstPassMinimumAboveTargetGoesOnFromItsPlacement: the same with
  pass 1 at overflow 0.27. The state is pass 1's, the overflow is pass
  1's and not stale, and the momentum and wirelength coefficients are
  pass 1's. Without the change they are the snapshot's.
- RevertToMinimumTest: a minimum at a later pass goes on from the
  routability snapshot's Nesterov state. It holds without the change;
  it states its scope.

The first two fail with the density on the coordinates instead of the
look-ahead coordinates, and with any one of the snapshot's members
(look-ahead coordinates, gradients, density penalty, step length, HPWL)
not restored, with the fillers' entries not kept through a cut and a
restore, and the third with the pass 1 condition dropped.

routability_first_pass_minimum places medium01 three times from the
def's placement: without routability, and with -routability_driven at a
target of 0.5 and -routability_check_overflow 0.10 and 0.30, where pass
1 runs at the target overflow and above it. No pass improves on the
first, and both routability runs end on the placement of the run
without the phase, instance by instance (HPWL 375,495.09 um, final
congestion 0.7418). Without this change, and with the density on the
coordinates, the run at 0.10 ends elsewhere and the test fails. About
30 s with one thread.

No other gpl regression ends on a first-pass minimum: the logs of
simple01-rd to simple04-rd (compared), upf_aes, place_ios_rd,
place_ios_td and congestion_inflation_default are byte-identical to
those of the change before this one.

Carried in bazel-orfs, not upstreamed; retires with the //:bump onto an
OpenROAD that has it.

